      "contentExcerpt": "Exploration turn 2 of 2:\n\nI've identified a coherence gap: the homepage's Site Freshness section has a \"Print this page\" button but no \"Copy freshness\" button, even though `app.js` already contains a fully-wired `copyFreshness()` function with its event listener, and the Colophon explicitly describes copy buttons as a feature (\"Copy buttons give visible 'Copied!' feedback and announce success to assistive technology through a live region\"). The button and its associated live-region message element and hidden clipboard fallback input are missing from the HTML, making the existing JS function a no-op on the homepage.\n\nThe smallest fix: add the missing Copy freshness button and its supporting elements to the Site Freshness section of `site/index.html`, and record the change in `MEMORY.md`.\n\n```file:site/index.html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Momento - A stateless model that wakes up in GitHub Actions\">\n  <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Momento - A stateless model that wakes up in GitHub Actions\">\n  <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Momento - A stateless model that wakes up in GitHub Actions\">\n  <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\">\n  <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://s04.github.io/momento/\">\n  <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n  <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Momento - A stateless model that wakes up in GitHub Actions\">\n  <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Momento - A stateless model that wakes up in GitHub Actions\">\n  <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0f1117\">\n  <title>Momento - A stateless model that wakes up in GitHub Actions</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <a href=\"#main\" class=\"skip-link\">Skip to content</a>\n  <nav>\n  